module gunbc.declared_side_refusal_cause_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust added to v1_interpreter when the heal publisher's
// 'status 200 undecodable' refusal was made diagnosable, enumerated because
// gunbc.seed_growth_admission makes unenumerated hand growth in src/v1 a stop-line.
//
// WHAT THE CHANGE IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. It is a RENDERING of a fact the interpreter already
// computed, not a new decision and not a second decode authority. The type-directed response decode
// already mints a RestResponseDecodeRefusal with a closed cause vocabulary
// (RestResponseDecodeCause: NoWireContract, AmbiguousWireContract, UnsupportedEncoding,
// UnsupportedNaming, NotAString, UnknownSpelling, and the rest); its Display exists but mixes
// DECLARED identifiers with values the response BODY presented (`spelling`, `json_text`, the wire
// spellings of an ambiguous arm), and the refusal string leaves the interpreter only as
// extdeps.transports.rest RestBodyUndecodable's `cause`, whose consumer is a publish path running
// with a credential in hand. So gunbc.heal_publication rest_refusal_text withheld the whole cause,
// and when every pull-request read on main began refusing at NoWireContract on PullRequestState
// (heal-publish runs 42795658738 and 42798626487, 2026-11-10) the runs carried no fact a human could
// read. rest_response_declared_cause answers from the same refusal the decode already produced and
// keeps only what is declared -- the cause kind, the coproduct, the encoding, the naming policy, the
// row count -- dropping every body-derived payload and the located field_path, which a record decode
// builds from the keys the object PRESENTED. Nothing is added to what may refuse, what may decode, or
// which row the decode consults; two renderings of one refusal now exist and the credential-path
// consumer reads the safe one.
//
// THE FAMILY GREW ONCE, BY THE SAME HAND AND FOR THE SAME MISSING FACT. A follow-up (#16253,
// 2026-11-10) found two of the four siblings still printing a sentence no one can act with: the
// uninhabited-member arm said how many members were left uninhabited and withheld their names, and
// the not-JSON arm could not tell a truncated or partial 200 -- the likeliest transient, and the one
// a replay of the same bytes cannot reproduce -- from a complete body that does not fit the
// declaration. Two items were added to serve those two renderers and nothing else: RestNullMembers,
// which carries the uninhabited names WITH the fact of whether the declaration vouches for every one
// of them, and rest_output_declared_field_names, which is how that is decided -- the operation's
// output children, resolved to authored names, the same projection the sibling
// rest_optional_output_field_names already uses for its own filter. Neither decides what refuses, and
// neither reads the body: one is a pair of names and a Bool, the other reads the declaration tree.
//
// THE FAMILY GREW A SECOND TIME, INWARD, TO PUT ONE WORDING ON ONE FACT (2026-11-11). The two claims
// in dag/test/claim/heal_publisher_provision_witness.dag that name BOTH spellings of a mis-spelled
// renamed member went red at 4aab999ddc37 -- this row's own commit. The renderer was installed in
// place of Display, and where Display's sentence named the authored spelling and the wire spelling,
// the renderer's named neither, so a heal-publish that refused for exactly the reason the model
// already knew published a line an operator could not act on. The repair adds two functions and
// removes no capability: rest_authored_name_sentence and rest_ambiguous_spelling_sentence, each
// String -> String -> String over the two names the decode read off the DECLARATION
// (authored_name_at / extract_from_key on the declared child), now called by BOTH renderers. They
// decide nothing, refuse nothing, and read nothing but their two arguments; they exist so the
// credential-path text and the Display text for these two causes cannot drift apart again -- a
// published line and its claims disagreed with no model change, because two renderers worded one
// cause. Two rows are added, for exactly those two functions, and nothing else.
//
// WHY IT IS RUST AND NOT .dag. The fact's vocabulary lives on the interpreter's side of the boundary:
// the cause enum is Rust, its payloads are Rust, and by the time a .dag can name the refusal the
// payloads are already one flat NonEmptyStr. Withholding or un-withholding at the .dag boundary can
// only be all-or-nothing, which is the defect being repaired. The renderer is therefore co-located
// with the enum it renders (gunbc.design_argument::single_authority: no second vocabulary is minted
// beside the first, and the Display impl is left intact for the paths that may echo a body).
//
// WHAT IS NOT COUNTED HERE, DISCLOSED. The test undecodable_cause_is_declared_side_only (a #[test]
// arm in v1_interpreter's test module, not a citable declaration) and the one-line edit at the mint
// site inside decide_rest_exchange, which now calls this renderer instead of formatting Display -- a
// call-site change in an existing declaration, not a newly authored one. The .dag side of the same
// change (the received-byte-count argument at the not-JSON mint site inside decide_rest_exchange, a
// one-line addition of an argument the call already had in hand -- body.as_bytes().len(), a length of
// the transport's own buffer, not a byte of the body -- and the two new arms of the same #[test] that
// plant FAKE-SECRET-MARKER in the parse message and in a body-shaped member set), and the .dag side of
// the same change (gunbc.heal_publication rest_refusal_text publishing the cause,
// test.claim.heal_publication_refusal_redaction_witness asserting the declared-side text, and
// test.claim.github_pull_request_decode_witness, whose recorded-body replay is what proves the cause
// is the fact the publisher needed) is .dag authority, not hand growth, and is not enumerated here.
//
// THE STANDING THE LANE OWES IT. gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing::v1_seed_standing admits a v1
// change that serves the v2 self-host program: this one restores the heal_workflow /
// heal_publisher_workflow loop, which is built from main and had refused every pull-request read.
// The second growth is disclosed the same way: the two arms of this enum's Display that now CALL the
// two sentence functions, and the two arms of the same #[test] that now assert the pair is PRESENT
// rather than absent, are edits inside existing declarations, not newly authored ones.
data declared_side_refusal_cause_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_response_declared_cause", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_body_read_refused_cause", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_body_not_json_cause", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_body_null_members_cause", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "RestNullMembers", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_output_declared_field_names", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_authored_name_sentence", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.v1_interpreter", decl_name: "rest_ambiguous_spelling_sentence", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "A refusal that a credential path may publish must be renderable from the DECLARED side alone, and the interpreter's existing cause vocabulary is the only place that knows which payloads are declared and which came from the body. The renderer adds no decision, no refusal and no decode path: it renders the refusal the decode already minted, so that withholding a cause is no longer the only safe option. Its own test plants FAKE-SECRET-MARKER in every value the four renderers refuse to publish -- the unknown spelling, the presented number text, the module wire_contract text, both spellings of a renamed member, the transport body-read text, the serde_json message, and the uninhabited member names -- and refuses if any of it reaches the published text, while the located declared field, the coproduct name and the declared encoding, naming policy and json kind are asserted to stay readable -- the path is an authored name out of the declaration tree (decode_json_by_declared_field seeds it from authored_name_at of the declared field), so publishing it costs no response content and is what a refusal is diagnosed from. The four are rendered together because gunbc.heal_publication rest_refusal_text publishes the cause for the whole RestBodyUndecodable arm: one place printing it means every place minting it must render it from declared facts, and a fifth renderer written by hand elsewhere would re-open the leak this one closes. The two items added by #16253 keep that rule rather than loosening it: the uninhabited member names are published only when EVERY one of them matches a child of the operation's declared output type, because map_response_to_value_json falls through to json_to_value when that type resolves to no children at all and then the record's keys are the ones the response presented -- a mixed or body-shaped record, and the case with no record at all, still publish a count and nothing else; and the not-JSON arm gained only a length out of the transport's buffer, while the serde_json message, which carries offsets into the body and sometimes the offending token, stays dropped.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete when the declared-side cause is not a hand renderer but a rendered projection: a realized wire vocabulary for RestResponseDecodeCause carrying its own safe-text member, so the interpreter's Display and the credential-path text are both projections of one declared inventory rather than a hand-written second match over the enum. Sufficient means the .dag vocabulary names every cause arm with its safe text -- including which members were left uninhabited and how many bytes arrived -- and a claim compares its coverage against the Rust enum, so a new arm cannot be added to one side and missed by the other; an interpreter-only match does not satisfy it.",
  current_boundary: "rest_response_declared_cause(refusal) -> String renders the cause kind, the coproduct's declared name, and only those payloads that are declared -- count, encoding, naming policy, json kind, and the two spellings of a mis-spelled renamed member, which the decode reads off the declaration and not from the body -- and returns text of the form 'body did not inhabit the declared output: <declared cause> at <located declared field> (<coproduct name>)' -- the shape dag/test/claim/rest_exchange_replay.dag pins, so it is not free to drift. It holds no state, reads nothing but the refusal it is given, and decides nothing: which body refuses, and why, stays entirely with the type-directed decode. Its three siblings cover the other mint sites of the same refusal: rest_body_read_refused_cause publishes fixed text and drops the transport's body-read text; rest_body_not_json_cause publishes fixed text plus how many bytes arrived, and drops the serde_json message it is handed; and rest_body_null_members_cause publishes a count, plus the member names when RestNullMembers says the declaration vouches for every one of them, and withholds them otherwise. The three shapes are pinned by dag/test/claim/rest_exchange_replay.dag, which requires the member name in the uninhabited arm and 'after 14 bytes received' in the not-JSON arm. The two renamed-member sentences have one owner each -- rest_authored_name_sentence and rest_ambiguous_spelling_sentence -- called by this renderer AND by the enum's Display, so a credential-path line and an echo-permitting line cannot word the same cause apart; each takes only the two declared names it prints, and dag/test/claim/heal_publisher_provision_witness.dag pins both sentences and requires that no value from the body reaches the credential-path text."
}
